  "dom_id": "step-q118442",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/997eb5cc08dcff78cb32f5b47b5d066546854b05f3b066953772e456e713d773.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could be used to describe the graph shown above?",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/1e532c806d81c3c4015d78f814dc4ea3fc3483f22d34ade385894df2e8e7e3c5.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin\u2061x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it across the $y$-axis.\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $5.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=5sin\u2061(-x).$\n\nNotice that, because the sine function is odd, the $y$-axis reflection has the same effect as the $x$-axis reflection, i.e.,\n\n$$\n5sin\u2061(-x)=-5sin\u2061x.\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=-5sin\u2061x.$ However, $y=-5sin\u2061x$ is not among the given options.",
